# Audit Report

## Verification contract status

All three contract items are satisfied with real, reproducible evidence.

### (a) `tests/loops/goal.test.ts` pins compaction event pauses watchdog
- File exists at `tests/loops/goal.test.ts` (5526 bytes), created by commit `84677bb5`
- Test asserts `continuation_start_paused_for_compaction` is in the ledger AND `continuation_start_unacknowledged` is NOT
- Test passes in 318.93ms in both isolated and full-suite runs

### (b) Genuine-stall warning still fires
- Second test in `tests/loops/goal.test.ts` asserts the inverse: `continuation_start_unacknowledged` IS in the ledger and `continuation_start_paused_for_compaction` is NOT
- Test passes in 317.38ms

### (c) `bun test` green, `npx tsc --noEmit` clean
- Full suite: **910 pass / 1 skip / 0 fail** in 48.32s across 80 files
- `npx tsc --noEmit` produced no output (clean)

### Implementation evidence

The watchdog fix in `extensions/loops/goal.ts`:
- `lastCompactionAt` declared at line 1293; set by `session_compact` handler at line 8318
- `__testOnlySetLastCompactionAt` hook at line 1303 (clean, non-recursive — does not spawn the test runner)
- `armContinuationStartWatchdog` (line 1865) checks `lastCompactionAt > (record.acceptedAt ?? 0)` and re-arms with `COMPACTION_REARM_CAP = 3` (3 × 150s = 7.5m hard ceiling)
- `continuation_start_paused_for_compaction` ledger event recorded with `{lastCompactionAt, acceptedAt, rearmCount, capped}`
- `clearCompactionRearms` invoked on watchdog clear (line 1722) and successful start (line 1823) — leak-free

The H-code clock-skew fix in `extensions/goal-loop-display.ts`:
- `auditorLastActivity` (line 384) and `auditorHasLiveEvidence` (line 443) both reject future timestamps
- Removes the misleading "0s ago" on stuck/skewed workers
- Verified at commit `cbd6ac3d`

## Reject-class check

Tests do NOT invoke `bun test` recursively. The watchdog regression uses `__testOnlySetLastCompactionAt(Date.now())` — a direct module-level setter — and inspects the ledger file. No fork-bomb, no recursion, no env sentinel needed.

## Verdicts on stated side-effect

The H-code fix (tasklist item #3) is a cheap, in-scope adjacent fix that closes a red test. The executor disclosed it explicitly. Acceptable engineering judgment.

